txtql::input::ambiguous

  × ambiguous match in rule `TEXT`: the text can be read in two ways with different results
   ╭─[input.txt:1:1]
 1 │ one two three
   · ───┬───┬
   ·    │   ╰── alternative: `first` = "one"
   ·    ╰── chosen: `first` = "one two"
   ╰────
  help: txtql picked the first reading, which gives {"first":"one two","rest":"three"}; the other
        gives {"first":"one","rest":"two three"}.
        Make the pattern more specific (literals, SPLITBY, LAZY) if the other reading was
        intended.
